      },
      "rev_n_3_1cbdc2_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_1cbdc2_0",
        "node_id": "n_3_1cbdc2",
        "thought_text": "Consider leap years and how they affect the distribution of days of the week across months.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794506371.3593242
      },
      "rev_n_1_7cd0e2_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_7cd0e2_1",
        "node_id": "n_1_7cd0e2",
        "thought_text": "Consider the total number of days in a non-leap year and how they distribute across the months. Specifically, analyze the cumulative days modulo 7 to see if the required conditions can be met.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_1_7cd0e2_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_882d0522c4",
        "created_at": 1794506380.198751
      },
      "rev_n_2_c0c872_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_c0c872_1",
        "node_id": "n_2_c0c872",
        "thought_text": "Consider the total number of days in a non-leap year, which is 365. Since there are 7 days in a week, 365 days modulo 7 equals 1. This means that after one year, the first day of the week shifts forward by one day. Therefore, for the first day of one month to be `day1` and the first day of the next month to be `day2`, the difference between `day1` and `day2` must be exactly 1 day apart in the weekly cycle. This can only happen if `day1` is followed immediately by `day2` in the sequence of days of the week.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_2_c0c872_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_d16e6ebfb0",
        "created_at": 1794506418.303361
      },
      "rev_n_3_1cbdc2_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_1cbdc2_1",
        "node_id": "n_3_1cbdc2",
        "thought_text": "Consider the properties of the Gregorian calendar and how the days of the week cycle through the months. Specifically, focus on the fact that a non-leap year has 365 days, which means there are 52 weeks and 1 extra day. This extra day affects the distribution of days of the week across the months. Additionally, analyze the specific constraints given in the problem to determine if the transition from one day to another within a single year is feasible.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_3_1cbdc2_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_3d44c28341",
        "created_at": 1794506430.5969064
      },
      "rev_n_4_7ffb60_0": {
